cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below, and also cite the data sources (Schilling et al. 2022; NHS Blood and Transplant for Study 2) and the registered analysis plans (Study 1, OSF, doi:10.17605/OSF.IO/PHQ42; Study 2, OSF, doi:10.17605/OSF.IO/VRH2U)."
title: "Demand forecasts versus a standing order for platelet ordering: a simulation study of public data from two hospitals, with a retrospectively registered analysis plan"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dixon
    given-names: Liam
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-0610-197X"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
version: "0.12.0"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dixonlj/Platelet-forecast"
abstract: "Code, results and manuscript (draft v11) for an educational, advisory-only simulation study comparing demand forecasts with a standing order for platelet ordering, using public aggregate data from University Hospital Aachen (CC BY 4.0) and the Stanford pip example data. Version 0.12.0 adds Study 2: a comparison of simple seasonal forecasting methods on national monthly platelet issues from NHS Blood and Transplant (England, 2016-2025), pre-registered on OSF before the analysis was run (doi:10.17605/OSF.IO/VRH2U). Its result was null: none of the three methods could be told apart from a same-month-last-year baseline under the pre-registered rule. The NHSBT spreadsheet is not included. Not a clinical tool and not ordering advice."
keywords:
  - platelet inventory
  - demand forecasting
  - waste
  - simulation
  - analysis plan
  - public data
  - blood bank
  - pre-registration
  - null result
